{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Who would have said to Abraham</b> — This is an expression of praise and greatness: see who he is and how great he is, who keeps His promise and promises and fulfills — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 21:7). And we do not find the word \"מִי\" used in such a manner for exaltation and honor, but only for contempt: \"Who is Abimelech, and who is Shechem?\" (Judges 9:28); \"Who is David, and who is the son of Jesse?\" (I Samuel 25:10). And what seems correct in my eyes is that she said: \"Elohim has made laughter for me; everyone who hears will laugh for me (יִצְחַק לִי)\" — to fill his mouth with rejoicing and laughter at the wonder performed for her. For who among all who hear would have said to Abraham at the outset, \"Sarah will nurse children\"? There is no one in the world who would say such a thing to him, even to comfort him, for this never entered the heart of any man. And the language of Onkelos (Onkelos on Genesis 21:7) is close to this: \"Who is the faithful one who said to Abraham and fulfilled: Sarah will nurse children\" — meaning, everyone who hears will laugh for me (יִצְחַק לִי), for there is no man who would be believed even in Abraham's eyes if he reported this wonder to him."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:21:26.827549607Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}